Mark changes of audio devices, and test when the echo controller restarts

WebRTC patch 0011 makes the echo controller anew at the next start of recording after a
change of audio devices. AudioDeviceImpl marks one (webrtc::MarkAudioDevicesChanged) when
an output or input is chosen other than the last asked for (on the worker thread, also
while playing or recording: the device's own restart there does not pass through the audio
state, and the next microphone turned on again makes it anew), and when the device module
tells of devices that came or went (OnDevicesUpdated).

test/echo_call.test.cc builds WebRTC's audio state with a real audio processing (an echo
controller that counts how it was made and restarted) and a mock audio device: a call's
start makes the echo controller anew, the first and every later one; a microphone turned
off and on again in the call restarts it, every time; a change of devices while it was off
makes it anew once, and one while recording runs counts at the next start too; a stream
heard coming or going while it was off, and recording turned off, make it anew;
a start of recording that fails makes and restarts nothing, and leaves the call and a
change it was told for the next start. Where the test expects a restart, a change marked
meanwhile by something else in the process (a real audio device module) makes it anew,
which the test accepts. AudioDeviceImpl marks another output or input chosen, not the same
one chosen again, and devices that came or went. Built in again: the library shows only
its own API.

